{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"printf 'error_rows=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$(grep -Ec '\"'\"'^'\"\\\\| [0-9]+ \\\\|' ERRORS.md)\\\"; printf 'error_open=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$(grep -Ec '\"'\"'^'\"\\\\| [0-9]+ .*\\\\| \\\\[ \\\\] \\\\|\"'$'\"' ERRORS.md)\\\"; rg -n 'STBDS_ASSERT' c_src/src/lib.c | wc -l; sed -n '1,120p' ERRORS.md\"","aggregated_output":"error_rows=21\nerror_open=21\n16\n# Error Surface\n\nThe C API does not define an error enum. Its recoverable rejection surface is\nmade of null/no-op returns and the `STBDS_INDEX_EMPTY` (`-1`) sentinel.\nAssertions reject corrupted internal state by aborting.\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | [ ] |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `stbds_hmfree_func` | `a == NULL` | return without action | [ ] |\n| 2 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | `a == NULL` | allocate zero default entry, set `*temp = -1`, return map pointer | [ ] |\n| 3 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | map exists but `hash_table == NULL` | set `*temp = -1`, return same map pointer | [ ] |\n| 4 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | key is absent from a populated hash table | set `*temp = -1`, return same map pointer | [ ] |\n| 5 | `stbds_hmget_key` | key is absent (the `_ts` rejection paths) | return map and store `temp = -1` in its header | [ ] |\n| 6 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `a == NULL` | return `NULL` | [ ] |\n| 7 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | map exists but `hash_table == NULL` | set header `temp = 0`, return same map | [ ] |\n| 8 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | key is absent from a populated hash table | set header `temp = 0`, return same map unchanged | [ ] |\n| 9 | `stbds_make_hash_index` (via put/mode) | threshold invariant `used_count_threshold + tombstone_count_threshold >= slot_count` | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n| 10 | `stbds_hmput_key` | post-growth invariant `i + 1 > arrcap(a)` | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n| 11 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | found slot is outside `table->slot_count` | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n| 12 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | decrement would make `used_count < 0` | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n| 13 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | moved final element cannot be found | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n| 14 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | moved element's slot does not point at `final_index` | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n| 15 | `stbds_stralloc` | after allocation, `len > a->remaining` | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n| 16 | `sh_geti` | lookup of `\"foo\"` in initial null map is not `-1` | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n| 17 | `sh_geti` | lookup of `\"foo\"` after selecting either string mode is not `-1` | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n| 18 | `sh_geti` | lookup of `\"foo\"` after setting default is not `-1` | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n| 19 | `sh_geti` | inserted even key does not map to `i*3`, or absent odd key does not map to `-2` | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n| 20 | `sh_geti` | after deleting keys `2 mod 4`, retained `0 mod 4` key is wrong or another key does not map to `-2` | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n| 21 | `sh_geti` | after deleting all keys, any lookup does not map to default `-2` | assertion failure/abort | [ ] |\n\nRows 9-21 are internal consistency assertions. No well-formed public FFI input\ncan make their predicates false; differential tests exercise each assertion\nsite with the valid state transitions that lead to it. Tests do not fabricate\nprivate allocator/hash metadata, because doing so is undefined behavior in C.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
