it set | [ ] |\n| 10 | `stbds_hash_string` | randomized multi-byte C strings and lengths | [ ] |\n| 11 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | zero length with a null data pointer | [ ] |\n| 12 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | tail lengths 1 through 7 (every switch arm), randomized bytes/seeds | [ ] |\n| 13 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | exact 8-byte blocks, including high-bit bytes | [ ] |\n| 14 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | one/many blocks plus tails 0 through 7; randomized lengths through 256 | [ ] |\n| 15 | `stbds_hmput_default` | null map creates one zeroed default entry | [ ] |\n| 16 | `stbds_hmput_default` | existing default entry is retained unchanged | [ ] |\n| 17 | `stbds_hmget_key`, `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | null/existing table-less map and absent key | [ ] |\n| 18 | `stbds_hmput_key`, `stbds_hmget_key`, `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | binary keys with key sizes 1, 4, 8, and 16; insert then found lookup | [ ] |\n| 19 | `stbds_hmput_key` | binary existing-key replacement path; item count/order unchanged | [ ] |\n| 20 | `stbds_hmput_key` | binary randomized many-entry insertion crossing 8-slot growth thresholds | [ ] |\n| 21 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | null, table-less, and populated map with missing binary key | [ ] |\n| 22 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | delete final binary entry (no move) | [ ] |\n| 23 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | delete non-final binary entry (move and slot-index repair) | [ ] |\n| 24 | `stbds_hmdel_key`, `stbds_hmput_key` | reuse a tombstone on later insertion | [ ] |\n| 25 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | many deletions trigger tombstone rebuild | [ ] |\n| 26 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | many deletions trigger table shrink | [ ] |\n| 27 | `stbds_shmode_func` | modes `STBDS_SH_NONE`/`DEFAULT`/`STRDUP`/`ARENA` and out-of-range `int` values | [ ] |\n| 28 | string map low-level API | default/reference string mode: empty, one, and many keys | [ ] |\n| 29 | string map low-level API | strdup mode: insert/update/get/delete/free with source buffers reused | [ ] |\n| 30 | string map low-level API | arena mode: insert/update/get/delete/free across arena blocks | [ ] |\n| 31 | string map low-level API | string lookups in populated tables: present and absent keys | [ ] |\n| 32 | `stbds_hmfree_func` | binary map, table-less map, each string ownership mode, and null | [ ] |\n| 33 | `stbds_stralloc` | empty/short strings fitting a new or existing 512-byte block | [ ] |\n| 34 | `stbds_stralloc` | string larger than current block with no prior storage | [ ] |\n| 35 | `stbds_stralloc` | oversized string with prior storage (side-block insertion branch) | [ ] |\n| 36 | `stbds_stralloc` | repeated allocations grow block exponent up to 1 MiB cap | [ ] |\n| 37 | `stbds_strreset` | empty and populated arena; all fields reset to zero | [ ] |\n| 38 | `strkey` | zero, positive, negative, `INT_MIN`, and `INT_MAX` | [ ] |\n| 39 | `sh_geti` | negative/zero, one, odd/even small counts, and randomized larger counts; both strdup and arena passes | [ ] |\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
